1. Read the old file's contents (if it doesn't exist → io error, which happens naturally
 with fs::read_to_string).
2. Split into 4 parts with splitn(4, SEP). If parts.len() != 4, return an error (
io::InvalidData or NotFound). Use std::io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::InvalidData,
 ...).
3. Reconstruct the content with new_id and new_title.
4. Write to dir/{new_id}.note.
5. Delete dir/{old_id}.note.

Edge: if old_id == new_id — in that case, writing and then deleting would delete the
 note. Handle: if old_id == new_id, only update the title in place. Handle this case
.

Also, if a note already exists with new_id and old_id != new_id: overwrite? The requirement
