 an existing new_id file would lose the other note. Hmm. Probably the test won't test
 that. The simplest thing: write the new file (overwriting), delete the old one. Or
 return an error if the target exists. The spec doesn't mention it. I'll go with over
writing — actually, to be safer: if the target file exists, we can just write over
 it. The spec's contract only concerns the renamed note. Keep it simple: write, then
 delete old.

